  "scope": "The hivm-enable-stride-align pass itself: mark normalization, demand propagation (up to allocations, down to leaves, union across op operands), the alloc re-padding rewrite with strided-view rewiring, the copy-based propagation-failure fallback, arch-dependent pad-dim selection (membase vs RegBase), and the membase-only hivm.storage_aligned metadata stamp. Excludes the internals of the producer passes (MarkStrideAlign / PreMarkStrideAlign — separate bundle) and of downstream consumers.",
  "related_entities": [
    { "name": "MarkStrideAlign (hivm-mark-stride-align)", "relation": "upstream producer of the stride-align marks this pass consumes" },
    { "name": "PreMarkStrideAlign (hivm-pre-mark-stride-align)", "relation": "regbase-only pre-pass marking vload roots to be spared from stride padding" },
    { "name": "memref FoldAllocReshape", "relation": "runs immediately before this pass inside alignStoragePipeline" },
    { "name": "AlignAllocSize (hivm-align-alloc-size)", "relation": "first pass of alignStoragePipeline, before the marking passes" },
    { "name": "hivm.storage_aligned (HIVM_StorageAligned attr)", "relation": "metadata contract this pass stamps on device functions, membase only" },
    { "name": "PropagateAlignUtil.cpp / AdjustAlignUtil.cpp / AlignBuffer Util.h", "relation": "shared helpers: mark creation, union/adjust of align info, shape computation, type propagation, copy fallback" },
    { "name": "hivm.hir.copy / UnrealizedConversionCastOp", "relation": "fallback machinery when aligned types cannot be propagated into a user" }
  ],
  "why_this_subject": "It is the consumer half of the mark/enable storage-align pair and the only place where the requested alignment becomes a real buffer layout: a whole-pipeline story about who demands alignment (marks), who decides the final buffer shapes (this pass), and what later lowering receives (padded allocs behind strided views). It also carries a clean arch fork (membase pads the next dim, RegBase pads the marked dim) and an unconditional-vs-gated pipeline subtlety worth teaching.",
